From 1141962f4e396c81dba7eb7b2f5ef69636e1fdde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:40:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(display): show provider-side tool calls as tool cards

A provider that runs a tool inside its own request (Anthropic's web
search through a subscription connector) can report each call in its
stream as delta.server_tool_events: a start with the call's arguments
and a completion with its result. Hermes never runs or replays these
calls. While the reply streams, each one fires the same tool start and
complete callbacks a Hermes tool does, so viewers show a tool card
(web_search: 'Searched the web for ...' with its results). The calls
are stored in the assistant row's display_metadata (never sent to a
model), and the transcript projection shows them as tool rows before
that reply, so a reload shows the same cards. A call whose result came
in a later reply shows once, with that result; one that no reply
answered (the provider dropped a search deferred past a client tool
call) closes as not run.
